      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure! Here’s a basic 4-week linear progression plan focusing on the squat, bench press, and deadlift. Make sure to warm up and stretch before each workout, and adjust the weights as suggested:\n\n**Week 1-4: Linear Progression Schedule**\n\n**Day 1: Squat**\n- Barbell Back Squat: 3 sets x 8 reps\n\n**Day 2: Rest or light cardio/stretching**\n\n**Day 3: Bench Press**\n- Barbell Bench Press: 3 sets x 8 reps\n\n**Day 4: Rest or light cardio/stretching**\n\n**Day 5: Deadlift**\n- Barbell Deadlift: 3 sets x 8 reps\n\n**Day 6: Rest or light cardio/stretching**\n\n**Day 7: Rest or active recovery (light cardio like walking/jogging)**\n\nAt the end of each week, increase the weight by 5-10 lbs for each exercise, ensuring you can complete the originally planned sets and reps with good form. Get plenty of rest between workouts on the same muscle group. Adjust as necessary for comfort and progress!",
