    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i'm a bit worried about how to handle the days when i'm feeling really exhausted or when the weight feels way too heavy to move. should i just push through it or is there a way to deal with that mental struggle during the lift?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's important to listen to your body, especially when you're new to lifting. Here's how you can handle those days:\n\n1. **Pushing Through 'Too Heavy':**\n   - Before you start lifting weights, try adjusting your grip width or stance to help distribute the weight more effectively.\n   - If after adjustments it still feels too difficult, drop to a bodyweight or light-set for that particular exercise.\n\n2. **Confronting Exhaustion:**\n   - Ensure you're fully hydrated and have eaten a good pre-workout meal.\n   - It’s okay to rest a bit longer before tackling these heavy or challenging lifts.\n   - Consider using rest periods between sets or decreasing the intensity of the workout for that day.\n\n3. **Adopting a Growth Mindset:**\n   - Remember that feeling uncomfortable sometimes means you're pushing outside your current limit and are more likely to grow.\n\n4. **Refocusing on Form:**\n   - Sometimes, fatigue can lead to compromised form, making your lifts more challenging. Take a moment to focus on your form before continuing.\n\n5. **Journaling Your Experience:**\n   - Writing down how you felt about those heavy days could help you identify any patterns and determine if there’s a specific aspect that",
      "source": "target",
